  "label": "Model Calibration From Heterogeneous Data",
  "related": [
    "pangenome-graphs-9c95",
    "untitled-topic-5b22",
    "assessment-enzyme-diversity-fermented-a0ca"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "missing-protein-protrec2-b54a",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and a published study benchmark likelihood-free and model-averaging methods for epidemic and phylodynamic calibration.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is calibration of explicit mechanistic epidemiological and phylodynamic models against data that are not simple scalar time series, including transmission-tree forests and viral sequence datasets. Likelihood-free inference recurs: ABC-SMC is presented as a practical PyMC tutorial for ecological and epidemiological dynamical systems, and Neural Posterior Estimation is evaluated on Ebola epidemiological and phylodynamic models. Other items examine how structural choices propagate into inference. A benchmark of fixed-tree-topology strategies on viral datasets finds substitution-model parameters robust, in contrast to clock rates and node ages. Bayesian model averaging over parametric coalescent growth models addresses structural uncertainty directly. A chi-square and PERMANOVA framework compares transmission-tree epidemic forests, with PERMANOVA more sensitive. The new element is explicit attention to which calibrated quantities depend on modeling assumptions, rather than reporting a single fitted parameter set. The pattern is not uniform across items; the forest comparison and the tutorial address different questions.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2025-11-29"
}
